AB  - Thyroid disease is the second largest disease in the endocrine field. SPECT imaging plays a vital role in recognizing difficult thyroid diseases. It is very important to develop the aided diagnosis of thyroid diseases based on SPECT images. A convolutional neural network (CNN) based computer aided diagnosis method was proposed for thyroid diseases using SPECT images. SPECT thyroid image data were collected to distinguish four kinds of thyroid diseases, including hyperthyroidism. hypothyroidism, methylene inflammation, and Hashimoto's disease. An improved CNN method with enhanced structure for deep learning was developed. Cross-layers were connected with channels in which trainable parameters were added to learn the feature weights of previous layer. Mixup, batch normalization, dropout and early stopping were employed to improve the performance of CNN. The proposed CNN method obtained the best accuracy and less error in confusion matrix, and the performance could be kept with different iteration number. The deep learning method can be efficiently applied to the diagnosis and analysis of thyroid SPECT images. The proposed CNN method has superior performance for diagnosis of thyroid diseases.
