AB  - Background: Computer-aided diagnosis based on chest X-ray (CXR) is an exponentially growing field of research owing to the development of deep learning, especially convolutional neural networks (CNNs). However, due to the intrinsic locality of convolution operations, CNNs cannot model long-range dependencies. Although vision transformers (ViTs) have recently been proposed to alleviate this limitation, those trained on patches cannot learn any dependencies for inter-patch pixels and thus, are insufficient for medical image detection. To address this problem, in this paper, we propose a CXR detection method which integrates CNN with a ViT for modeling patch-wise and inter-patch dependencies.
