AB  - Change of Arteriolar-to-Venular diameter Ratio (AVR) can reflect signs of many ophthalmic diseases such as cataract, glaucoma and diabetic retinopathy. Therefore vessel extraction and quantitative analysis of vascular width in ocular fundus images play important roles in facilitating clinical diagnosis. An automatic measurement method of Arteriolar-to-Venular Diameter Ratio is proposed. First, vessel extraction and measurement are performed combining Hessian matrix multi-scale analysis, and Hessian matrix has advantages of for detecting line-like structure. Then, a General Regression Neural Network (GRNN) classifier is utilized to classify artery and vein. Finally, AVR in the Region of Interest (ROI) is calculated. The proposed segmentation method can not only guarantee continuity of blood vessels, but also segment thick main blood vessels and capillaries. The proposed measurement method can accurate measure vascular bifurcation diameter, and obtain diameters of artery and vein automatically, as well as AVR in ROI. The proposed method is tested on REVIEW and DRIVE database and the results show that it is highly effective.
