AB  - For medical images, the accuracy of the segmentation results is crucial for doctors to diagnose the disease and give the correct treatment plan. BP neural network was used to segment medical images. First, the mapping relationship of BP neural network is used to find the best adaptive function through the powerful search function of the corresponding BP neural network. Then, the BP neural network obtains the best output value, calculates the threshold, and divides the image area by the threshold. In this paper, the biological image analysis method is used to record and analyze the evoked potentials generated by visual search before and after fatigue, and the comparative analysis of the indicators that are more sensitive to general visual search is P300, P100, and N170. The results show that the latency of P300 is significantly shortened and the amplitude of the wave is decreased when pictures without target stimulation are identified. When identifying pictures with target stimuli, the latency of P100 and P300 significantly prolonged (p < 0.05), and the amplitude of volatility decreased, indicating that the visual search and information processing transmission of the subject were delayed. The amount of attention devoted has decreased. The experimental results show that the improved algorithm can get a clearer image segmentation effect, improve the image segmentation accuracy, and have important reference significance for clinical diagnosis.
