AB  - Recent advancements in imaging technologies are poised to redefine the diagnostic and therapeutic role of radiology. In part 2 of this review series, we outline emerging innovations with transformative clinical potential, including photon-counting detector CT for ultrahigh-resolution, spectral imaging; ultra-high-field MRI systems (>= 7 T); and the expanding field of theranostics. We also examine nanotechnology-enhanced imaging agents, the integration of AI-driven opportunistic screening, and radiogenomics to enable precision diagnostics and early disease detection. Together, these developments represent a paradigm shift toward more personalized, data-rich, and preventative imaging approaches. Challenges in implementation, such as safety, cost, and workflow integration, are discussed with an emphasis on collaboration and infrastructure to support sustained clinical translation. (c) 2026 The Association of Academic Radiology. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.
